title HUNK85 — the faceted query: OR within a facet, AND across facets
prompt recur the itinerary loop — take the next agent-doable Lindy-first crux-first lap after HUNK84, send each finished increment as its own signed round
think After HUNK84 brought the OR to glass, the boolean algebra stood whole as AND and OR separately — yet a real facet sidebar runs on both at once, in a fixed shape: OR within one facet (stainless or brass), AND across different facets (that union, and under a dollar). That is the canonical faceted query, a conjunction of disjunctions (CNF), and it was the next in-layer crux.
think Chose a grammar that carries the two levels plainly and stays backward-compatible: the line is space-separated groups, each group a `|`-separated disjunction. A `|`-free line is an AND of one-clause groups — exactly HUNK78's conjunction — so the new grammar is a strict superset that disturbs nothing already proven.
think No new matching rule: a group is HUNK83's matches_any over its `|`-clauses, and the line is those group verdicts under AND, exactly as HUNK78 ANDs single clauses. FacetQuery holds an array of part_or.OrQuery groups; filter_facets keeps a part when every group matches_any.
think Three laws pin it honest: backward-compatibility (filter_facets over a `|`-free line equals part_and.filter_and part for part), identity (empty line = match-all, the AND identity; a hand-built empty group = match-none, the OR identity), and distribution ((a|b) AND c == (a AND c) union (b AND c), checked over every part).
obs Witness GREEN; TAME style bans clean; width-check exit 0. HUNK83 disjunction and HUNK78 conjunction re-run GREEN beneath. Custody gate #3 untouched — a price clause compares a recorded cent count, nothing moved; no network, key, or funds.
obs Synced image/README.md marketplace section — the boolean query algebra now reads HUNK75–HUNK85, naming the faceted grammar and its witness, a docs-implementation ratchet on a file already open for this journey.
